  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "A durable public portfolio",
      "items": [
        "CloudFront and S3 remain independent of EKS. DEMO has synthetic data and no API origin.",
        "AWS forwarding was proven, then removed. A failed AWS request never falls back to synthetic data."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Authorization is not just a JWT",
      "items": [
        "The REQUEST authorizer authenticates protected routes. The integration overwrites trusted identity headers.",
        "Shipment and Tracking validate proxy trust and call Auth with the original bearer token. Subject binding, current roles and ownership fail closed.",
        "Tracking uses a separate internal credential for Shipment ownership lookup. Internal HTTP is not mTLS."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Control is separate from request traffic",
      "items": [
        "LBC owns the ALB, target registration and target-health readiness conditions. These are control actions, not a request proxy.",
        "ESO reads Secrets Manager and writes Kubernetes Secrets. Each Deployment consumes secretKeyRef environment values; migration Jobs use separate credentials.",
        "The asynchronous Tracking → EventBridge → SQS → Shipment path has its own diagram."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Evidence and current state",
      "items": [
        "DECLARED: arrows describe source-backed design; the reading guide gives the source for each relationship.",
        "OBSERVED: topology captured on 28–29 October 2026. Runtime retired on 29 October; RDS retained stopped.",
        "PROVEN applies only to named experiments. These diagrams are not live telemetry or a production certification."
      ]
    }
  ],
